IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa20-part26`
IMPORT `coa20-part26a`

-- coa20-part27-merger.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 27 (Mergers and divisions of public companies), Chapters 1 and 2,
-- ss 902 to 918A, lines 12528-12800 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. LAYER 1, objective.
-- Every requirement section answers a `s 903(1) status of a requirement` (complied with / not complied with / does not apply / not covered)
-- so that a requirement switched off by an excluding section is never read as complied with. An excluding section answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN:
-- JUST TRUE = the requirement does not apply, JUST FALSE = it does, NOTHING = not known. Facts a witness can state are BOOLEAN, DATE or NUMBER;
-- answers of other sections of this Part (or other parts) are MAYBE BOOLEAN inputs named for the answering section.
-- Periods: "one month before" is the library's calendar month (`add months`, which clamps the day), and "the period beginning one month
-- before, and ending on, the date" includes both ends (fork F6).

-- A requirement switched off by an excluding section (a "subject to" signpost, instantiated below).

-- An exclusion that applies when its gate is met ("In a case where ..., the requirements of ... do not apply").

GIVEN `first day of continuous availability` IS A DATE
      `last day of continuous availability` IS A DATE
      `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` MEANS
    `first day of continuous availability` AT MOST (`s 906(3) the date one month before` `the date`) AND `last day of continuous availability` AT LEAST `the date`

GIVEN date IS A DATE
      months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 910(1) the date a number of months before` MEANS `add months` date (0 MINUS months)

-- ===========================================================================================================
§ `Part 27 -- Mergers and divisions of public companies`
-- ===========================================================================================================

§§ `Application of this Part (s 902)`

-- JURAL none (a rule fixing the scope of the Part)
-- src:12531 | (1) This Part applies where—
-- src:12532 | (a) a compromise or arrangement is proposed between a public company and—
-- src:12533 | (i) its creditors or any class of them, or
-- src:12534 | (ii) its members or any class of them,
-- src:12535 | for the purposes of, or in connection with, a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies or the amalgamation of any two or more companies,
-- src:12536 | (b) the scheme involves—
-- src:12537 | (i) a merger (as defined in section 904), or
-- src:12538 | (ii) a division (as defined in section 919), and
-- src:12539 | (c) the consideration for the transfer (or each of the transfers) envisaged is to be shares in the transferee company (or one or more of the transferee companies) receivable by members of the transferor company (or transferor companies), with or without any cash payment to members.
@ref s 902(1) The Part applies to a scheme of merger or division of a public company where shares are the consideration (src:12531-12539)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a compromise or arrangement is proposed between the public company and its creditors, or any class of them, or its members, or any class of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the compromise or arrangement is proposed for the purposes of, or in connection with, a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies or the amalgamation of any two or more companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 904(1) the scheme involves a merger` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 919(1) the scheme involves a division` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the consideration for the transfer (or each of the transfers) is to be shares in the transferee company (or one or more of the transferee companies) receivable by members of the transferor company (or transferor companies), with or without any cash payment to members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 902(1) this Part applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 4(2) the company is a public company`
                AND `a compromise or arrangement is proposed between the public company and its creditors, or any class of them, or its members, or any class of them`
                AND `the compromise or arrangement is proposed for the purposes of, or in connection with, a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies or the amalgamation of any two or more companies`
                AND `the consideration for the transfer (or each of the transfers) is to be shares in the transferee company (or one or more of the transferee companies) receivable by members of the transferor company (or transferor companies), with or without any cash payment to members`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part applies where— (a) a compromise or arrangement is proposed between a public company and ..., (b) ..., and (c) the consideration for the transfer ... is to be shares" (an unmet "where")
        OTHERWISE `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 904(1) the scheme involves a merger`, `s 919(1) the scheme involves a division`) -- (b) "the scheme involves (i) a merger ..., or (ii) a division": either yes is yes, both no is no, otherwise not known

-- src:12540 | (2) In this Part—
-- src:12541 | (a) a “new company” means a company formed for the purposes of, or in connection with, the scheme, and
-- src:12542 | (b) an “existing company” means a company other than one formed for the purposes of, or in connection with, the scheme.
@ref s 902(2) "new company" and "existing company" (src:12540-12542)
GIVEN `the company is formed for the purposes of, or in connection with, the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 902(2)(a) the company is a new company` MEANS
    IF `the company is formed for the purposes of, or in connection with, the scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “new company” means a company formed for the purposes of, or in connection with, the scheme"

GIVEN `the company is formed for the purposes of, or in connection with, the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 902(2)(b) the company is an existing company` MEANS
    IF `the company is formed for the purposes of, or in connection with, the scheme`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an “existing company” means a company other than one formed for the purposes of, or in connection with, the scheme"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- JURAL the members and creditors of the company being wound up: immunity from Part 27 | whoever proposes the scheme: disability
-- src:12543 | (3) This Part does not apply where the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed is being wound up.
@ref s 902(3) The Part does not apply where the company is being wound up (src:12543)
GIVEN `the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 902(3) the winding up of the company takes the compromise or arrangement out of this Part` MEANS
    IF `the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed is being wound up`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Part does not apply where the company ... is being wound up" says nothing of a company that is not

§§ `Relationship of this Part to Parts 26 and 26A (s 903)`

-- Part 27 bars the court from sanctioning under Part 26 or 26A until the relevant requirements are complied with. The answer is a bar, not a power:
-- JUST FALSE = a bar stands (a requirement is not complied with); JUST TRUE = Part 27 does not bar; NOTHING = a requirement is not covered.
-- JURAL the members and creditors of the companies: claim that the court not sanction until the requirements are complied with | the court: disability to sanction
-- src:12545 | (1) The court must not sanction the compromise or arrangement under Part 26 (arrangements and reconstructions: general) or Part 26A (arrangements and reconstructions: companies in financial difficulty) unless the relevant requirements of this Part have been complied with.
@ref s 903(1) The court must not sanction under Part 26 or 26A unless the relevant requirements of Part 27 have been complied with (src:12545)
GIVEN statuses IS A LIST OF `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 903(1) the requirements of this Part do not bar the court from sanctioning` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` statuses
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court must not sanction the compromise or arrangement under Part 26 ... or Part 26A ... unless the relevant requirements of this Part have been complied with"
        IF elem `s 903(1) requirement not covered` statuses
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a requirement's status is not covered (an excluding provision or a fact is not known)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12546 | (2) The requirements applicable to a merger are specified in sections 905 to 914.
-- src:12547 | Certain of those requirements, and certain general requirements of Parts 26 and 26A, are modified or excluded by the provisions of sections 915 to 918A.
@ref s 903(2) The requirements applicable to a merger are in sections 905 to 914, modified or excluded by sections 915 to 918A (src:12546-12547)
GIVEN `the statuses of the requirements of sections 905 to 914 as modified or excluded by sections 915 to 918A` IS A LIST OF `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 903(2) the requirements applicable to a merger do not bar the court from sanctioning` MEANS
    `s 903(1) the requirements of this Part do not bar the court from sanctioning` `the statuses of the requirements of sections 905 to 914 as modified or excluded by sections 915 to 918A`

-- src:12548 | (3) The requirements applicable to a division are specified in sections 920 to 930.
-- src:12549 | Certain of those requirements, and certain general requirements of Parts 26 and 26A, are modified or excluded by the provisions of sections 931 to 934.
@ref s 903(3) The requirements applicable to a division are in sections 920 to 930, modified or excluded by sections 931 to 934 (src:12548-12549)
GIVEN `the statuses of the requirements of sections 920 to 930 as modified or excluded by sections 931 to 934` IS A LIST OF `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 903(3) the requirements applicable to a division do not bar the court from sanctioning` MEANS
    `s 903(1) the requirements of this Part do not bar the court from sanctioning` `the statuses of the requirements of sections 920 to 930 as modified or excluded by sections 931 to 934`

§§ `Mergers and merging companies (s 904)`

DECLARE `s 904(1) kind of merger` IS ONE OF
    `s 904(1)(a) a merger by absorption`
    `s 904(1)(b) a merger by formation of a new company`

-- JURAL none (a definition)
-- src:12553 | (1) The scheme involves a merger where under the scheme—
-- src:12554 | (a) the undertaking, property and liabilities of one or more public companies, including the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed, are to be transferred to another existing public company (a “merger by absorption”), or
-- src:12555 | (b) the undertaking, property and liabilities of two or more public companies, including the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed, are to be transferred to a new company, whether or not a public company, (a “merger by formation of a new company”).
@ref s 904(1) The scheme involves a merger (src:12553-12555)
GIVEN `s 904(1)(a) the scheme involves a merger by absorption` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 904(1)(b) the scheme involves a merger by formation of a new company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 904(1) the scheme involves a merger` MEANS
    `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 904(1)(a) the scheme involves a merger by absorption`, `s 904(1)(b) the scheme involves a merger by formation of a new company`)

@ref s 904(1)(a) A merger by absorption (src:12553-12554)
GIVEN `the undertaking, property and liabilities of one or more public companies, including the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed, are to be transferred under the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are to be transferred to another existing public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 904(1)(a) the scheme involves a merger by absorption` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking, property and liabilities of one or more public companies, including the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed, are to be transferred under the scheme` AND `they are to be transferred to another existing public company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The scheme involves a merger where under the scheme— (a) the undertaking, property and liabilities of one or more public companies ... are to be transferred to another existing public company"

@ref s 904(1)(b) A merger by formation of a new company (src:12555)
GIVEN `the undertaking, property and liabilities of two or more public companies, including the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed, are to be transferred under the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are to be transferred to a new company, whether or not a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 904(1)(b) the scheme involves a merger by formation of a new company` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking, property and liabilities of two or more public companies, including the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed, are to be transferred under the scheme` AND `they are to be transferred to a new company, whether or not a public company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the undertaking, property and liabilities of two or more public companies ... are to be transferred to a new company, whether or not a public company"

-- src:12556 | (2) References in this Part to “the merging companies” are—
-- src:12557 | (a) in relation to a merger by absorption, to the transferor and transferee companies;
-- src:12558 | (b) in relation to a merger by formation of a new company, to the transferor companies.
@ref s 904(2) "the merging companies" (src:12556-12558)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 904(1) kind of merger`
      `the company is a transferor company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is the transferee company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 904(2) the company is one of the merging companies` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 904(1)(a) a merger by absorption` THEN
        IF `the company is a transferor company` OR `the company is the transferee company` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this Part to “the merging companies” are— (a) in relation to a merger by absorption, to the transferor and transferee companies"
    WHEN `s 904(1)(b) a merger by formation of a new company` THEN
        IF `the company is a transferor company` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in relation to a merger by formation of a new company, to the transferor companies"

§§ `Draft terms of scheme (merger) (s 905)`

-- JURAL the members and creditors: claim to draft terms | the directors of the merging companies: duty to draw them up and adopt them
-- src:12561 | (1) A draft of the proposed terms of the scheme must be drawn up and adopted by the directors of the merging companies.
@ref s 905(1) A draft of the proposed terms must be drawn up and adopted by the directors of the merging companies (src:12561)
GIVEN `a draft of the proposed terms of the scheme has been drawn up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been adopted by the directors of every one of the merging companies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 905(1) the draft terms have been drawn up and adopted` MEANS
    IF `a draft of the proposed terms of the scheme has been drawn up` AND `it has been adopted by the directors of every one of the merging companies`
    THEN `s 903(1) requirement complied with`
    ELSE `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` -- a bare "must" not done (fork F3)

-- (a)(i)-(iii) per company (taken as true only if given for each transferor company and the transferee company); (b), (c), (d) may be left out where s 915(2) applies.
-- JURAL the members: claim to the particulars | the directors of the merging companies: duty to give them
-- src:12562 | (2) The draft terms must give particulars of at least the following matters—
-- src:12563 | (a) in respect of each transferor company and the transferee company—
-- src:12564 | (i) its name,
-- src:12565 | (ii) the address of its registered office, and
-- src:12566 | (iii) whether it is a company limited by shares or a company limited by guarantee and having a share capital;
-- src:12567 | (b) the number of shares in the transferee company to be allotted to members of a transferor company for a given number of their shares (the “share exchange ratio”) and the amount of any cash payment;
-- src:12568 | (c) the terms relating to the allotment of shares in the transferee company;
-- src:12569 | (d) the date from which the holding of shares in the transferee company will entitle the holders to participate in profits, and any special conditions affecting that entitlement;
-- src:12570 | (e) the date from which the transactions of a transferor company are to be treated for accounting purposes as being those of the transferee company;
-- src:12571 | (f) any rights or restrictions attaching to shares or other securities in the transferee company to be allotted under the scheme to the holders of shares or other securities in a transferor company to which any special rights or restrictions attach, or the measures proposed concerning them;
-- src:12572 | (g) any amount of benefit paid or given or intended to be paid or given—
-- src:12573 | (i) to any of the experts referred to in section 909 (expert's report), or
-- src:12574 | (ii) to any director of a merging company,
-- src:12575 | and the consideration for the payment of benefit.
@ref s 905(2) The draft terms must give particulars of at least the listed matters (src:12562-12575)
GIVEN `s 915(2) the draft terms need not give the particulars in section 905(2)(b), (c) and (d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the name of each transferor company and of the transferee company is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address of the registered office of each is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `whether each is a company limited by shares or a company limited by guarantee and having a share capital is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share exchange ratio and the amount of any cash payment are given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms relating to the allotment of shares in the transferee company are given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date from which the holding of shares in the transferee company will entitle the holders to participate in profits, and any special conditions affecting that entitlement, are given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date from which the transactions of a transferor company are to be treated for accounting purposes as being those of the transferee company is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any rights or restrictions attaching to shares or other securities in the transferee company to be allotted to holders of securities with special rights or restrictions, or the measures proposed concerning them, are given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any amount of benefit paid or given or intended to be paid or given to any of the experts or to any director of a merging company, and the consideration for the payment of benefit, are given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 905(2) the draft terms give the particulars required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 915(2) the draft terms need not give the particulars in section 905(2)(b), (c) and (d)` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN `s 903(1) requirement not covered` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 915 relieves the draft terms of (b), (c) and (d) is not known
        IF `the name of each transferor company and of the transferee company is given` AND `the address of the registered office of each is given`
           AND `whether each is a company limited by shares or a company limited by guarantee and having a share capital is given`
           AND `the date from which the transactions of a transferor company are to be treated for accounting purposes as being those of the transferee company is given`
           AND `any rights or restrictions attaching to shares or other securities in the transferee company to be allotted to holders of securities with special rights or restrictions, or the measures proposed concerning them, are given`
           AND `any amount of benefit paid or given or intended to be paid or given to any of the experts or to any director of a merging company, and the consideration for the payment of benefit, are given`
           AND (`s 915(2) the draft terms need not give the particulars in section 905(2)(b), (c) and (d)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                OR (`the share exchange ratio and the amount of any cash payment are given`
                    AND `the terms relating to the allotment of shares in the transferee company are given`
                    AND `the date from which the holding of shares in the transferee company will entitle the holders to participate in profits, and any special conditions affecting that entitlement, are given`))
            THEN `s 903(1) requirement complied with`
        OTHERWISE `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` -- a bare "must ... give particulars of at least" not done (fork F3)

-- JURAL none (a signpost whose effect is section 915)
-- src:12576 | (3) The requirements in subsection (2)(b), (c) and (d) are subject to section 915 (circumstances in which certain particulars not required).
@ref s 905(3) The requirements in subsection (2)(b), (c) and (d) are subject to section 915 (src:12576)
GIVEN `s 915(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 905(3) the requirements in subsection (2)(b), (c) and (d) are subject to section 915` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 915(1) this section applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 915 does not apply on these facts, and the subsection says nothing else
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 915 applies is not known

§§ `Publication of draft terms by registrar (merger) (s 906)`

-- JURAL the registrar (receipt of the draft terms): none | the directors of each merging company: duty to deliver a copy
-- src:12578 | (1) The directors of each of the merging companies must deliver a copy of the draft terms to the registrar.
@ref s 906(1) The directors of each merging company must deliver a copy of the draft terms to the registrar (src:12578)
GIVEN `s 906A(1) section 906 does not apply in respect of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the directors of the company have delivered a copy of the draft terms to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 906(1) the directors have delivered a copy of the draft terms to the registrar` MEANS
    `s 903(1) the status of the requirement` `s 906A(1) section 906 does not apply in respect of the company` `the directors of the company have delivered a copy of the draft terms to the registrar`

-- JURAL the members and creditors: claim to publication of notice of receipt | the registrar: duty to publish (an official: no seat)
-- src:12579 | (2) The registrar must publish in the Gazette notice of receipt by him from that company of a copy of the draft terms.
@ref s 906(2) The registrar must publish in the Gazette notice of receipt of a copy of the draft terms (src:12579)
GIVEN `the registrar has received from the company a copy of the draft terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar has published notice of receipt in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 906(2) the registrar has published notice of receipt of the draft terms in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the registrar has received from the company a copy of the draft terms`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "notice of receipt by him from that company of a copy of the draft terms" (no copy received)
    ELSE IF `the registrar has published notice of receipt in the Gazette`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar must publish in the Gazette notice of receipt" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

-- "at least one month before the date of any meeting": the notice date plus one calendar month is on or before the meeting date. No meeting summoned: not covered.
-- src:12580 | (3) That notice must be published at least one month before the date of any meeting of that company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme.
@ref s 906(3) The notice must be published at least one month before the date of any meeting summoned to approve the scheme (src:12580)
GIVEN `date the notice was published in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 906(3) the notice was published at least one month before the meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `date of the first meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before the date of any meeting of that company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme" (no meeting is summoned)
    WHEN JUST meeting THEN
        IF `s 906(3) the date one month before` meeting AT LEAST `date the notice was published in the Gazette`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be published at least one month before the date of any meeting"

-- JURAL none (a signpost whose effect is section 906A)
-- src:12581 | (4) The requirements in this section are subject to section 906A (publication of draft terms on company website).
@ref s 906(4) The requirements in section 906 are subject to section 906A (src:12581)
GIVEN `s 906A(1) section 906 does not apply in respect of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 906(4) the requirements in section 906 are subject to section 906A` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 906A(1) section 906 does not apply in respect of the company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 906A does not apply on these facts, and the subsection says nothing else
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 906A applies is not known

§§ `Publication of draft terms on company website (merger) (s 906A)`

-- The first condition: the draft terms are on a website maintained by or on behalf of the company, which identifies it.
-- src:12584 | (2) The first condition is that the draft terms are made available on a website which—
-- src:12585 | (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and
-- src:12586 | (b) identifies the company.
@ref s 906A(2) The first condition: the draft terms are on the company's website (src:12584-12586)
GIVEN `the draft terms are made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the website identifies the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 906A(2) the first condition is met` MEANS
    IF `the draft terms are made available on a website` AND `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` AND `the website identifies the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first condition is that the draft terms are made available on a website which— (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and (b) identifies the company"

-- src:12587 | (3) The second condition is that neither access to the draft terms on the website nor the supply of a hard copy of them from the website is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted.
@ref s 906A(3) The second condition: access and the supply of a hard copy are not conditional on a fee or otherwise restricted (src:12587)
GIVEN `access to the draft terms on the website is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supply of a hard copy of them from the website is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 906A(3) the second condition is met` MEANS
    IF NOT (`access to the draft terms on the website is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted` OR `the supply of a hard copy of them from the website is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second condition is that neither access to the draft terms on the website nor the supply of a hard copy of them from the website is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted"

-- src:12588 | (4) The third condition is that the directors of the company deliver to the registrar a notice giving details of the website.
@ref s 906A(4) The third condition: the directors deliver to the registrar a notice giving details of the website (src:12588)
GIVEN `the directors of the company have delivered to the registrar a notice giving details of the website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 906A(4) the third condition is met` MEANS
    IF `the directors of the company have delivered to the registrar a notice giving details of the website`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The third condition is that the directors of the company deliver to the registrar a notice giving details of the website"

-- src:12589 | (5) The fourth condition is that the registrar publishes the notice in the Gazette at least one month before the date of any meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme.
@ref s 906A(5) The fourth condition: the registrar publishes the notice in the Gazette at least one month before the meeting (src:12589)
GIVEN `date the registrar published the notice in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 906A(5) the fourth condition is met` MEANS
    IF `s 906(3) the date one month before` `date of the first meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme` AT LEAST `date the registrar published the notice in the Gazette`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The fourth condition is that the registrar publishes the notice in the Gazette at least one month before the date of any meeting"

-- The fifth condition: available throughout the period [one month before the meeting, the meeting], unless s 940A disregards the failure.
-- src:12590 | (6) The fifth condition is that the draft terms remain available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date of any such meeting.
@ref s 906A(6) The fifth condition: the draft terms remain available on the website throughout the period (src:12590)
GIVEN `first day of continuous availability` IS A DATE
      `last day of continuous availability` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme` IS A DATE
      `s 940A(1) the failure to make the draft terms available throughout the period is to be disregarded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 906A(6) the fifth condition is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day of continuous availability` `last day of continuous availability` `date of the first meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 940A(1) the failure to make the draft terms available throughout the period is to be disregarded` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- s 940A: the failure "is to be disregarded"
        IF `s 940A(1) the failure to make the draft terms available throughout the period is to be disregarded` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 940A disregards the failure is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The fifth condition is that the draft terms remain available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date of any such meeting"

-- JURAL the company: immunity from section 906 | the registrar: disability to require delivery and publication
-- src:12583 | (1) Section 906 does not apply in respect of a company if the conditions in subsections (2) to (6) are met.
@ref s 906A(1) Section 906 does not apply in respect of a company if the conditions in subsections (2) to (6) are met (src:12583)
GIVEN `s 906A(2) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 906A(3) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 906A(4) the third condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 906A(5) the fourth condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 906A(6) the fifth condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 906A(1) section 906 does not apply in respect of the company` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) (LIST `s 906A(2) the first condition is met`, `s 906A(3) the second condition is met`, `s 906A(4) the third condition is met`, `s 906A(5) the fourth condition is met`, `s 906A(6) the fifth condition is met`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 906 does not apply in respect of a company if the conditions in subsections (2) to (6) are met" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
        IF elem NOTHING (LIST `s 906A(2) the first condition is met`, `s 906A(3) the second condition is met`, `s 906A(4) the third condition is met`, `s 906A(5) the fourth condition is met`, `s 906A(6) the fifth condition is met`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known and none has failed
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Approval of members of merging companies (s 907)`

-- One class of members at a meeting: the number present and voting, the number for, and the value present and voting and for.
DECLARE `s 907(1) votes of a class of members` HAS
    `s 907(1) number present and voting` IS A NUMBER
    `s 907(1) number for the scheme` IS A NUMBER
    `s 907(1) value present and voting` IS A NUMBER
    `s 907(1) value for the scheme` IS A NUMBER

-- A majority in number (more than half) representing 75% in value (at least 75%), present and voting in person or by proxy; every class of each merging company.
-- JURAL the members of each merging company: right to vote on the scheme | the directors and the company: duty to put it to them; the scheme: no effect without the approval
-- src:12592 | (1) The scheme must be approved by a majority in number, representing 75% in value, of each class of members of each of the merging companies, present and voting either in person or by proxy at a meeting.
@ref s 907(1) The scheme must be approved by a majority in number, representing 75% in value, of each class of members of each of the merging companies (src:12592)
GIVEN `s 907(2) the meeting of members is not required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      classes IS A LIST OF `s 907(1) votes of a class of members`
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 907(1) the scheme has been approved by the members of the merging company` MEANS
    `s 903(1) the status of the requirement` `s 907(2) the meeting of members is not required`
        (all (GIVEN class YIELD 2 TIMES class's `s 907(1) number for the scheme` GREATER THAN class's `s 907(1) number present and voting`
                                AND class's `s 907(1) value for the scheme` AT LEAST (0.75 TIMES class's `s 907(1) value present and voting`)) classes)

-- src:12593 | (2) This requirement is subject to sections 916, 917, 917A and 918 (circumstances in which meetings of members not required).
@ref s 907(2) The requirement is subject to sections 916, 917, 917A and 918 (src:12593)
GIVEN `s 916(2) the meeting of members of the transferee company is not required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 917(2) the meeting of members of any of the merging companies is not required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 917A(1) the meeting of members of the transferor company is not required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 918(1) the meeting of members of the transferee company is not required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 907(2) the meeting of members is not required` MEANS
    `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 916(2) the meeting of members of the transferee company is not required`, `s 917(2) the meeting of members of any of the merging companies is not required`, `s 917A(1) the meeting of members of the transferor company is not required`, `s 918(1) the meeting of members of the transferee company is not required`)

§§ `Directors' explanatory report (merger) (s 908)`

-- JURAL the members: claim to the report | the directors of each merging company: duty to draw it up and adopt it
-- src:12595 | (1) The directors of each of the merging companies must draw up and adopt a report.
@ref s 908(1) The directors of each merging company must draw up and adopt a report (src:12595)
GIVEN `s 908(3) the requirement in section 908 is excluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the directors of the company have drawn up and adopted a report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 908(1) the directors have drawn up and adopted a report` MEANS
    `s 903(1) the status of the requirement` `s 908(3) the requirement in section 908 is excluded` `the directors of the company have drawn up and adopted a report`

-- (2)(b): "insofar as that statement does not deal with the following matters, a further statement": the grounds and the valuation difficulties may be in either.
-- src:12596 | (2) The report must consist of—
-- src:12597 | (a) the required statement explaining the effect of the compromise or arrangement, and
-- src:12598 | (b) insofar as that statement does not deal with the following matters, a further statement—
-- src:12599 | (i) setting out the legal and economic grounds for the draft terms, and in particular for the share exchange ratio, and
-- src:12600 | (ii) specifying any special valuation difficulties.
@ref s 908(2) The report must consist of the required statement and, insofar as it does not deal with them, a further statement (src:12596-12600)
GIVEN `the report includes the required statement explaining the effect of the compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the required statement sets out the legal and economic grounds for the draft terms, and in particular for the share exchange ratio` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the required statement specifies any special valuation difficulties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a further statement sets out the legal and economic grounds for the draft terms, and in particular for the share exchange ratio` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a further statement specifies any special valuation difficulties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 908(2) the report consists of what the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the report includes the required statement explaining the effect of the compromise or arrangement`
       AND (`the required statement sets out the legal and economic grounds for the draft terms, and in particular for the share exchange ratio` OR `a further statement sets out the legal and economic grounds for the draft terms, and in particular for the share exchange ratio`)
       AND (`the required statement specifies any special valuation difficulties` OR `a further statement specifies any special valuation difficulties`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The report must consist of— (a) the required statement ..., and (b) insofar as that statement does not deal with the following matters, a further statement" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

DECLARE `s 908(2A) the statement required` IS ONE OF
    `s 908(2A)(a) the statement required by section 897`
    `s 908(2A)(b) the statement required by section 901D`

-- src:12601 | (2A) In subsection (2) “the required statement explaining the effect of the compromise or arrangement” means—
-- src:12602 | (a) in a case where a meeting is summoned under section 896 in relation to the compromise or arrangement, the statement required by section 897;
-- src:12603 | (b) in a case where a meeting is summoned under section 901C in relation to the compromise or arrangement, the statement required by section 901D.
@ref s 908(2A) "the required statement explaining the effect of the compromise or arrangement" (src:12601-12603)
GIVEN `a meeting is summoned under section 896 in relation to the compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a meeting is summoned under section 901C in relation to the compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 908(2A) the statement required`
`s 908(2A) the required statement explaining the effect of the compromise or arrangement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a meeting is summoned under section 896 in relation to the compromise or arrangement` AND NOT (`a meeting is summoned under section 901C in relation to the compromise or arrangement`)
            THEN JUST `s 908(2A)(a) the statement required by section 897`
        IF `a meeting is summoned under section 901C in relation to the compromise or arrangement` AND NOT (`a meeting is summoned under section 896 in relation to the compromise or arrangement`)
            THEN JUST `s 908(2A)(b) the statement required by section 901D`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a case where a meeting is summoned under section 896 ...; in a case where a meeting is summoned under section 901C": neither, or both, is said to be the case

-- src:12604 | (3) The requirement in this section is subject to section 915 (circumstances in which reports not required) , section 915A (other circumstances in which reports and inspection not required) and section 918A (agreement to dispense with reports etc)..
@ref s 908(3) The requirement is subject to sections 915, 915A and 918A (src:12604)
GIVEN `s 915(4) the requirements of sections 908 and 909 do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 915A(2) the requirements of sections 908, 909, 910, 911 and 911B do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 918A(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 908(3) the requirement in section 908 is excluded` MEANS
    `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 915(4) the requirements of sections 908 and 909 do not apply`, `s 915A(2) the requirements of sections 908, 909, 910, 911 and 911B do not apply`, `s 918A(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement`)

§§ `Expert's report (merger) (s 909)`

-- JURAL the members: claim to an expert's report | each merging company: duty to have one drawn up
-- src:12606 | (1) An expert's report must be drawn up on behalf of each of the merging companies.
-- src:12607 | (2) The report required is a written report on the draft terms to the members of the company.
@ref s 909(1) An expert's report must be drawn up on behalf of each merging company: a written report on the draft terms to the members (src:12606-12607)
GIVEN `s 909(7) the requirement in section 909 is excluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a written report on the draft terms to the members of the company has been drawn up on its behalf by an expert` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 909(1) an expert's report has been drawn up on behalf of the company` MEANS
    `s 903(1) the status of the requirement` `s 909(7) the requirement in section 909 is excluded` `a written report on the draft terms to the members of the company has been drawn up on its behalf by an expert`

-- JURAL the merging companies (jointly): power to apply for a joint expert | the court: liability to hear it
-- src:12608 | (3) The court may on the joint application of all the merging companies approve the appointment of a joint expert to draw up a single report on behalf of all those companies.
-- src:12609 | If no such appointment is made, there must be a separate expert's report to the members of each merging company drawn up by a separate expert appointed on behalf of that company.
@ref s 909(3) The court may on the joint application of all the merging companies approve a joint expert; otherwise a separate expert for each (src:12608-12609)
GIVEN `the court has approved the appointment of a joint expert on the joint application of all the merging companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a single report has been drawn up by the joint expert on behalf of all the merging companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a separate expert's report to the members of each merging company has been drawn up by a separate expert appointed on behalf of that company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 909(3) the way the expert's report is drawn up complies` MEANS
    IF `the court has approved the appointment of a joint expert on the joint application of all the merging companies`
    THEN (IF `a single report has been drawn up by the joint expert on behalf of all the merging companies`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text allows the court's approval of a joint expert and does not say a separate report is then forbidden
    ELSE (IF `a separate expert's report to the members of each merging company has been drawn up by a separate expert appointed on behalf of that company`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no such appointment is made, there must be a separate expert's report to the members of each merging company drawn up by a separate expert"

-- JURAL none (a rule fixing who may be the expert)
-- src:12610 | (4) The expert must be a person who—
-- src:12611 | (a) is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor (see section 1212), and
-- src:12612 | (b) meets the independence requirement in section 936.
@ref s 909(4) The expert must be eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor and meet the independence requirement (src:12610-12612)
GIVEN `s 1212 the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 936(1) the person meets the independence requirement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 909(4) the person may be the expert` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 1212 the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 936(1) the person meets the independence requirement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The expert must be a person who— (a) is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor ..., and (b) meets the independence requirement in section 936"
        IF `s 1212 the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 936(1) the person meets the independence requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 1212 or section 936 is not answered

-- (e) applies only to a valuation made by a person other than the expert (section 935).
-- src:12613 | (5) The expert's report must—
-- src:12614 | (a) indicate the method or methods used to arrive at the share exchange ratio;
-- src:12615 | (b) give an opinion as to whether the method or methods used are reasonable in all the circumstances of the case, indicate the values arrived at using each such method and (if there is more than one method) give an opinion on the relative importance attributed to such methods in arriving at the value decided on;
-- src:12616 | (c) describe any special valuation difficulties that have arisen;
-- src:12617 | (d) state whether in the expert's opinion the share exchange ratio is reasonable; and
-- src:12618 | (e) in the case of a valuation made by a person other than himself (see section 935), state that it appeared to him reasonable to arrange for it to be so made or to accept a valuation so made.
@ref s 909(5) What the expert's report must contain (src:12613-12618)
GIVEN `the report indicates the method or methods used to arrive at the share exchange ratio` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report gives an opinion on whether the method or methods used are reasonable, indicates the values arrived at using each method and, if there is more than one, gives an opinion on their relative importance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report describes any special valuation difficulties that have arisen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether in the expert's opinion the share exchange ratio is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a valuation was made by a person other than the expert` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states that it appeared to the expert reasonable to arrange for it to be so made or to accept a valuation so made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 909(5) the expert's report contains what the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the report indicates the method or methods used to arrive at the share exchange ratio`
       AND `the report gives an opinion on whether the method or methods used are reasonable, indicates the values arrived at using each method and, if there is more than one, gives an opinion on their relative importance`
       AND `the report describes any special valuation difficulties that have arisen`
       AND `the report states whether in the expert's opinion the share exchange ratio is reasonable`
       AND ((NOT (`a valuation was made by a person other than the expert`)) OR `the report states that it appeared to the expert reasonable to arrange for it to be so made or to accept a valuation so made`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The expert's report must— (a) indicate the method or methods ...; (e) in the case of a valuation made by a person other than himself ..., state that it appeared to him reasonable" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

-- JURAL the expert: claim of access to documents and to information from the officers | the merging companies and their officers: duty to give them
-- src:12619 | (6) The expert (or each of them) has—
-- src:12620 | (a) the right of access to all such documents of all the merging companies, and
-- src:12621 | (b) the right to require from the companies' officers all such information,
-- src:12622 | as he thinks necessary for the purposes of making his report.
@ref s 909(6) The expert has a right of access to documents and to require information from the officers (src:12619-12622)
GIVEN `the person is the expert (or one of the experts)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expert thinks the document or information necessary for the purposes of making his report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 909(6) the expert has the right of access to the document or to require the information` MEANS
    IF `the person is the expert (or one of the experts)` AND `the expert thinks the document or information necessary for the purposes of making his report`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The expert (or each of them) has ... all such documents ... as he thinks necessary for the purposes of making his report"

-- src:12623 | (7) The requirement in this section is subject to section 915 (circumstances in which reports not required) , section 915A (other circumstances in which reports and inspection not required)and section 918A (agreement to dispense with expert's report) .
@ref s 909(7) The requirement is subject to sections 915, 915A and 918A (src:12623)
GIVEN `s 915(4) the requirements of sections 908 and 909 do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 915A(2) the requirements of sections 908, 909, 910, 911 and 911B do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 918A(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 909(7) the requirement in section 909 is excluded` MEANS
    `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 915(4) the requirements of sections 908 and 909 do not apply`, `s 915A(2) the requirements of sections 908, 909, 910, 911 and 911B do not apply`, `s 918A(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement`)

§§ `Supplementary accounting statement (merger) (s 910)`

-- (1)(a): the last annual accounts relate to a financial year that ended before the date seven months before the first meeting; (b) if no meeting is
-- required (ss 916 to 918): before the date six months before the directors adopt the draft terms. NOTHING for the meeting date means no meeting is required.
-- src:12625 | (1) This section applies if the last annual accounts of any of the merging companies relate to a financial year ending before—
-- src:12626 | (a) the date seven months before the first meeting of the company summoned for the purposes of approving the scheme, or
-- src:12627 | (b) if no meeting of the company is required (by virtue of any of sections 916 to 918), the date six months before the directors of the company adopt the draft terms of the scheme.
@ref s 910(1) The section applies if the last annual accounts relate to a financial year ending too long before (src:12625-12627)
GIVEN `the end of the financial year to which the last annual accounts relate` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of the company summoned for the purposes of approving the scheme` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date the directors of the company adopt the draft terms of the scheme` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 910(1) this section applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `date of the first meeting of the company summoned for the purposes of approving the scheme`
    WHEN JUST meeting THEN
        IF `the end of the financial year to which the last annual accounts relate` LESS THAN (`s 910(1) the date a number of months before` meeting 7)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies if the last annual accounts of any of the merging companies relate to a financial year ending before— (a) the date seven months before the first meeting"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the end of the financial year to which the last annual accounts relate` LESS THAN (`s 910(1) the date a number of months before` `date the directors of the company adopt the draft terms of the scheme` 6)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if no meeting of the company is required (by virtue of any of sections 916 to 918), the date six months before the directors of the company adopt the draft terms of the scheme"

-- JURAL the members: claim to a supplementary accounting statement | the directors: duty to prepare it
-- src:12628 | (1A) If the company has not made public a half-yearly financial report relating to a period ending on or after the date mentioned in subsection (1), the directors of the company must prepare a supplementary accounting statement.
@ref s 910(1A) If the company has not made public a half-yearly financial report for a period ending on or after that date, the directors must prepare a statement (src:12628)
GIVEN `s 910(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 910(6) the requirement in section 910 is excluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company has made public a half-yearly financial report relating to a period ending on or after the date mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors of the company have prepared a supplementary accounting statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 910(1A) the directors have prepared a supplementary accounting statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 910(1) this section applies` EQUALS NOTHING THEN `s 903(1) requirement not covered` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is not known
        IF `s 910(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN `s 903(1) requirement does not apply` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies if"
        IF `the company has made public a half-yearly financial report relating to a period ending on or after the date mentioned in subsection (1)` THEN `s 903(1) requirement does not apply` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company has not made public a half-yearly financial report"
        OTHERWISE `s 903(1) the status of the requirement` `s 910(6) the requirement in section 910 is excluded` `the directors of the company have prepared a supplementary accounting statement`

-- (2)(a): a balance sheet as at a date not more than three months before the draft terms were adopted. A date after the adoption is not covered by the text.
-- src:12629 | (2) That statement must consist of—
-- src:12630 | (a) a balance sheet dealing with the state of affairs of the company as at a date not more than three months before the draft terms were adopted by the directors, and
-- src:12631 | (b) where the company would be required under section 399 to prepare group accounts if that date were the last day of a financial year, a consolidated balance sheet dealing with the state of affairs of the company and the undertakings that would be included in such a consolidation.
@ref s 910(2) The statement must consist of a balance sheet and, where group accounts would be required, a consolidated balance sheet (src:12629-12631)
GIVEN `the date as at which the balance sheet deals with the state of affairs of the company` IS A DATE
      `date the draft terms were adopted by the directors` IS A DATE
      `s 399 the company would be required to prepare group accounts if that date were the last day of a financial year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement includes a consolidated balance sheet dealing with the state of affairs of the company and the undertakings that would be included in such a consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 910(2) the statement consists of what the section requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date as at which the balance sheet deals with the state of affairs of the company` GREATER THAN `date the draft terms were adopted by the directors`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text speaks of a date "not more than three months before the draft terms were adopted", not of a later date
        IF `the date as at which the balance sheet deals with the state of affairs of the company` LESS THAN (`s 910(1) the date a number of months before` `date the draft terms were adopted by the directors` 3)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a balance sheet dealing with the state of affairs of the company as at a date not more than three months before the draft terms were adopted"
        IF `s 399 the company would be required to prepare group accounts if that date were the last day of a financial year` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 399 (group accounts) is outside this range
        IF `s 399 the company would be required to prepare group accounts if that date were the last day of a financial year` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND NOT (`the statement includes a consolidated balance sheet dealing with the state of affairs of the company and the undertakings that would be included in such a consolidation`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where the company would be required under section 399 to prepare group accounts ..., a consolidated balance sheet"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12632 | (3) The requirements of this Act ... as to the balance sheet forming part of a company's annual accounts, and the matters to be included in notes to it, apply to the balance sheet required for an accounting statement under this section, with such modifications as are necessary by reason of its being prepared otherwise than as at the last day of a financial year.
