§§ `Inspection of documents (merger) (s 911)`

-- (2): "the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date of the first meeting".
-- src:12640 | (2) The period referred to above is the period—
-- src:12641 | (a) beginning one month before, and
-- src:12642 | (b) ending on the date of,
-- src:12643 | the first meeting of the members, or any class of members, of the company for the purposes of approving the scheme.
@ref s 911(2) The period is the month up to the date of the first meeting of members (src:12640-12643)
GIVEN `first day on which the members could inspect and obtain copies` IS A DATE
      `last day on which the members could inspect and obtain copies` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of the members, or any class of members, of the company for the purposes of approving the scheme` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 911(2) the members could inspect and obtain copies throughout the period` MEANS
    `s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day on which the members could inspect and obtain copies` `last day on which the members could inspect and obtain copies` `date of the first meeting of the members, or any class of members, of the company for the purposes of approving the scheme`

-- JURAL the members of each merging company: claim to inspect the documents and to have copies free of charge | each merging company: duty to allow it
-- src:12637 | (1) The members of each of the merging companies must be able, during the period specified below—
-- src:12638 | (a) to inspect at the registered office of that company copies of the documents listed below relating to that company and every other merging company, and
-- src:12639 | (b) to obtain copies of those documents or any part of them on request free of charge.
@ref s 911(1) The members of each merging company must be able during the period to inspect the documents and to obtain copies free of charge (src:12637-12639)
GIVEN `s 911(7) the requirements in section 911 are excluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the members could inspect at the registered office of the company, throughout the period, copies of the documents listed in subsection (3) relating to that company and every other merging company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the members could obtain copies of those documents or any part of them on request free of charge throughout the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 911(1) the members could inspect the documents and obtain copies` MEANS
    `s 903(1) the status of the requirement` `s 911(7) the requirements in section 911 are excluded`
        (`the members could inspect at the registered office of the company, throughout the period, copies of the documents listed in subsection (3) relating to that company and every other merging company`
         AND `the members could obtain copies of those documents or any part of them on request free of charge throughout the period`)

DECLARE `s 911(3) document the members must be able to inspect` IS ONE OF
    `s 911(3)(a) the draft terms`
    `s 911(3)(b) the directors' explanatory report`
    `s 911(3)(c) the expert's report`
    `s 911(3)(d) the company's annual accounts and reports for the last three financial years ending on or before the first meeting`
    `s 911(3)(e) any supplementary accounting statement required by section 910`
    `s 911(3)(f) a recent half-yearly financial report made public instead of the statement`

-- (3)(e) is a document only if section 910 requires a statement; (3)(f) only where no statement is required because a half-yearly report was made public.
-- Subsection (4): the requirements of (3)(b) and (c) are subject to sections 915 and 918A, so those two documents drop out where `s 911(4)` says so.
-- src:12644 | (3) The documents referred to above are—
-- src:12645 | (a) the draft terms;
-- src:12646 | (b) the directors' explanatory report;
-- src:12647 | (c) the expert's report;
-- src:12648 | (d) the company's annual accounts and reports for the last three financial years ending on or before the first meeting of the members, or any class of members, of the company summoned for the purposes of approving the scheme; . . .
-- src:12649 | (e) any supplementary accounting statement required by section 910.; and
-- src:12650 | (f) if no statement is required by section 910 because the company has made public a recent half-yearly financial report (see subsection (1A) of that section), that report.
@ref s 911(3) The documents (src:12644-12650)
GIVEN document IS A `s 911(3) document the members must be able to inspect`
      `s 911(4) the requirements of subsection (3)(b) and (c) are excluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a supplementary accounting statement is required by section 910` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no statement is required by section 910 because the company has made public a recent half-yearly financial report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 911(3) the document is one the members must be able to inspect` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `s 911(3)(a) the draft terms` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 911(3)(b) the directors' explanatory report` THEN
        CONSIDER `s 911(4) the requirements of subsection (3)(b) and (c) are excluded`
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirements of subsection (3)(b) and (c) are subject to section 915 ... and section 918A" (the exclusion applies)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 915 or 918A excludes the document is not known
    WHEN `s 911(3)(c) the expert's report` THEN
        CONSIDER `s 911(4) the requirements of subsection (3)(b) and (c) are excluded`
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirements of subsection (3)(b) and (c) are subject to section 915 ... and section 918A" (the exclusion applies)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 915 or 918A excludes the document is not known
    WHEN `s 911(3)(d) the company's annual accounts and reports for the last three financial years ending on or before the first meeting` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 911(3)(e) any supplementary accounting statement required by section 910` THEN
        IF `a supplementary accounting statement is required by section 910` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any supplementary accounting statement required by section 910"
    WHEN `s 911(3)(f) a recent half-yearly financial report made public instead of the statement` THEN
        IF `no statement is required by section 910 because the company has made public a recent half-yearly financial report` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if no statement is required by section 910 because the company has made public a recent half-yearly financial report"

-- JURAL none (a signpost whose effect is section 911A(1))
-- src:12651 | (3A) The requirement in subsection (1)(a) is subject to section 911A(1) (publication of documents on company website).
@ref s 911(3A) The requirement in subsection (1)(a) is subject to section 911A(1) (src:12651)
GIVEN `s 911A(1) section 911(1)(a) does not apply to the document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 911(3A) the requirement in section 911(1)(a) is subject to section 911A(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 911A(1) section 911(1)(a) does not apply to the document`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 911A(1) does not apply on these facts, and the subsection says nothing else
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 911A(1) applies is not known

-- src:12652 | (4) The requirements of subsection (3)(b) and (c) are subject to section 915 (circumstances in which reports not required) and section 918A (agreement to dispense with reports etc).
@ref s 911(4) The requirements of subsection (3)(b) and (c) are subject to sections 915 and 918A (src:12652)
GIVEN `s 915(5) the requirements of section 911 so far as relating to a document required to be drawn up under sections 908 and 909 do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 918A(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 911(4) the requirements of subsection (3)(b) and (c) are excluded` MEANS
    `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 915(5) the requirements of section 911 so far as relating to a document required to be drawn up under sections 908 and 909 do not apply`, `s 918A(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement`)

-- JURAL the member (who consented to electronic communication): immunity from the right to hard copy | the company: disability under section 1145
-- src:12653 | (5) Section 1145 (right to hard copy) does not apply to a document sent or supplied in accordance with subsection (1)(b) to a member who has consented to information being sent or supplied by the company by electronic means and has not revoked that consent.
@ref s 911(5) Section 1145 (right to hard copy) does not apply to a document supplied under subsection (1)(b) to a member who has consented to electronic means (src:12653)
GIVEN `the document is sent or supplied in accordance with subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member has consented to information being sent or supplied by the company by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member has not revoked that consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 911(5) section 1145 does not apply to the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is sent or supplied in accordance with subsection (1)(b)` AND `the member has consented to information being sent or supplied by the company by electronic means` AND `the member has not revoked that consent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to a document sent or supplied in accordance with subsection (1)(b) to a member who has consented ... and has not revoked that consent"

-- src:12654 | (6) Part 4 of Schedule 5 (communications by means of a website) does not apply for the purposes of subsection (1)(b) (but see section 911A(5)).
@ref s 911(6) Part 4 of Schedule 5 (communications by means of a website) does not apply for the purposes of subsection (1)(b) (src:12654)
GIVEN `the purpose is that of subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 911(6) Part 4 of Schedule 5 does not apply` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is that of subsection (1)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply for the purposes of subsection (1)(b) (but see section 911A(5))"

-- src:12655 | (7) The requirements in this section are subject to section 915A (other circumstances in which reports and inspection not required).
@ref s 911(7) The requirements in this section are subject to section 915A (src:12655)
GIVEN `s 915A(2) the requirements of sections 908, 909, 910, 911 and 911B do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 911(7) the requirements in section 911 are excluded` MEANS
    `s 915A(2) the requirements of sections 908, 909, 910, 911 and 911B do not apply`

§§ `Publication of documents on company website (merger) (s 911A)`

-- src:12658 | (2) The first condition is that the document is made available on a website which—
-- src:12659 | (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and
-- src:12660 | (b) identifies the company.
@ref s 911A(2) The first condition: the document is on the company's website (src:12658-12660)
GIVEN `the document is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the website identifies the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 911A(2) the first condition is met` MEANS
    IF `the document is made available on a website` AND `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` AND `the website identifies the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first condition is that the document is made available on a website which— (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and (b) identifies the company"

-- src:12661 | (3) The second condition is that access to the document on the website is not conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted.
@ref s 911A(3) The second condition: access to the document is not conditional on a fee or otherwise restricted (src:12661)
GIVEN `access to the document on the website is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 911A(3) the second condition is met` MEANS
    IF NOT (`access to the document on the website is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted`) THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second condition is that access to the document on the website is not conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted"

-- src:12662 | (4) The third condition is that the document remains available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date of any meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme.
@ref s 911A(4) The third condition: the document remains available throughout the period (src:12662)
GIVEN `first day of continuous availability` IS A DATE
      `last day of continuous availability` IS A DATE
      `date of any meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme` IS A DATE
      `s 940A(1) the failure to make the document available throughout the period is to be disregarded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 911A(4) the third condition is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day of continuous availability` `last day of continuous availability` `date of any meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 940A(1) the failure to make the document available throughout the period is to be disregarded` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- s 940A: the failure "is to be disregarded"
        IF `s 940A(1) the failure to make the document available throughout the period is to be disregarded` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 940A disregards the failure is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The third condition is that the document remains available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date of any meeting"

-- (6): where members can obtain copies only as mentioned in subsection (5), section 911(1)(a) applies even if the conditions are met.
-- JURAL the member: claim to inspect at the registered office (unless the website conditions are met) | the company: duty to allow inspection or to meet the conditions
-- src:12657 | (1) Section 911(1)(a) does not apply to a document if the conditions in subsections (2) to (4) are met in relation to that document. This is subject to subsection (6).
@ref s 911A(1) Section 911(1)(a) does not apply to a document if the conditions in subsections (2) to (4) are met, subject to subsection (6) (src:12657)
GIVEN `s 911A(2) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 911A(3) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 911A(4) the third condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 911A(6) members can obtain copies only as mentioned in subsection (5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 911A(1) section 911(1)(a) does not apply to the document` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 911A(6) members can obtain copies only as mentioned in subsection (5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where members of a company are able to obtain copies of a document only as mentioned in subsection (5), section 911(1)(a) applies to that document even if the conditions in subsections (2) to (4) are met"
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) (LIST `s 911A(2) the first condition is met`, `s 911A(3) the second condition is met`, `s 911A(4) the third condition is met`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 911(1)(a) does not apply to a document if the conditions in subsections (2) to (4) are met" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
        IF elem NOTHING (LIST `s 911A(2) the first condition is met`, `s 911A(3) the second condition is met`, `s 911A(4) the third condition is met`, `s 911A(6) members can obtain copies only as mentioned in subsection (5)`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer is not known and no condition has failed
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- JURAL the person: claim to a copy he can retain and print | the company: duty to keep the document on the website so that he can
-- src:12663 | (5) A person is able to obtain a copy of a document as required by section 911(1)(b) if—
-- src:12664 | (a) the conditions in subsections (2) and (3) are met in relation to that document, and
-- src:12665 | (b) the person is able, throughout the period specified in subsection (4)—
-- src:12666 | (i) to retain a copy of the document as made available on the website, and
-- src:12667 | (ii) to produce a hard copy of it.
@ref s 911A(5) A person is able to obtain a copy as section 911(1)(b) requires if the first two conditions are met and he can retain and print it (src:12663-12667)
GIVEN `s 911A(2) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 911A(3) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is able, throughout the period specified in subsection (4), to retain a copy of the document as made available on the website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is able, throughout that period, to produce a hard copy of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 911A(5) the person is able to obtain a copy as section 911(1)(b) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 911A(2) the first condition is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 911A(3) the second condition is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is able to obtain a copy of a document as required by section 911(1)(b) if— (a) the conditions in subsections (2) and (3) are met" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
        IF NOT (`the person is able, throughout the period specified in subsection (4), to retain a copy of the document as made available on the website` AND `the person is able, throughout that period, to produce a hard copy of it`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the person is able, throughout the period specified in subsection (4)— (i) to retain a copy ..., and (ii) to produce a hard copy of it"
        IF `s 911A(2) the first condition is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 911A(3) the second condition is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known

-- src:12668 | (6) Where members of a company are able to obtain copies of a document only as mentioned in subsection (5), section 911(1)(a) applies to that document even if the conditions in subsections (2) to (4) are met.
@ref s 911A(6) Where copies can be obtained only as mentioned in subsection (5), section 911(1)(a) applies even if the conditions are met (src:12668)
GIVEN `members of the company are able to obtain copies of the document only as mentioned in subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 911A(6) members can obtain copies only as mentioned in subsection (5)` MEANS
    IF `members of the company are able to obtain copies of the document only as mentioned in subsection (5)` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where members of a company are able to obtain copies of a document only as mentioned in subsection (5)"

§§ `Report on material changes of assets of merging companies (s 911B)`

-- src:12670 | (1) The directors of each of the merging companies must report—
-- src:12671 | (a) to every meeting of the members, or any class of members, of that company summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme, and
-- src:12672 | (b) to the directors of every other merging company,
-- src:12673 | any material changes in the property and liabilities of that company between the date when the draft terms were adopted and the date of the meeting in question.
@ref s 911B(1) The directors of each merging company must report material changes in property and liabilities to meetings and to the other companies' directors (src:12670-12673)
GIVEN `s 911B(3) the requirement in section 911B is excluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the directors have reported to every meeting of the members, or any class of members, summoned to agree to the scheme any material changes in the property and liabilities of the company between the date when the draft terms were adopted and the date of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have reported those changes to the directors of every other merging company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 911B(1) the directors have reported material changes in property and liabilities` MEANS
    `s 903(1) the status of the requirement` `s 911B(3) the requirement in section 911B is excluded`
        (`the directors have reported to every meeting of the members, or any class of members, summoned to agree to the scheme any material changes in the property and liabilities of the company between the date when the draft terms were adopted and the date of the meeting` AND `the directors have reported those changes to the directors of every other merging company`)

-- src:12674 | (2) The directors of each of the other merging companies must in turn—
-- src:12675 | (a) report those matters to every meeting of the members, or any class of members, of that company summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme, or
-- src:12676 | (b) send a report of those matters to every member entitled to receive notice of such a meeting.
@ref s 911B(2) The directors of each of the other merging companies must in turn report those matters to the meeting or send a report to every member entitled to notice (src:12674-12676)
GIVEN `s 911B(3) the requirement in section 911B is excluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the directors have reported those matters to every meeting of the members, or any class of members, summoned to agree to the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have sent a report of those matters to every member entitled to receive notice of such a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 911B(2) the directors of the other merging companies have reported those matters in turn` MEANS
    `s 903(1) the status of the requirement` `s 911B(3) the requirement in section 911B is excluded`
        (`the directors have reported those matters to every meeting of the members, or any class of members, summoned to agree to the scheme` OR `the directors have sent a report of those matters to every member entitled to receive notice of such a meeting`)

-- src:12677 | (3) The requirement in this section is subject to section 915A (other circumstances in which reports and inspection not required) and section 918A (agreement to dispense with reports etc ).
@ref s 911B(3) The requirement is subject to sections 915A and 918A (src:12677)
GIVEN `s 915A(2) the requirements of sections 908, 909, 910, 911 and 911B do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 918A(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 911B(3) the requirement in section 911B is excluded` MEANS
    `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 915A(2) the requirements of sections 908, 909, 910, 911 and 911B do not apply`, `s 918A(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement`)

§§ `Approval of articles of new transferee company (merger) (s 912)`

-- (1) merger by formation of a new company: ordinary resolution of each transferor company, unless (2): under Part 26A, not the company in respect of which the compromise is proposed.
-- The text shows ". . ." in subsection (1) before "each of the transferor companies" (an omission).
-- src:12679 | (1) In the case of a merger by formation of a new company, the articles of the transferee company, or a draft of them, must be approved by ordinary resolution of . . . each of the transferor companies. This is subject to subsection (2).
-- src:12680 | (2) In the case of a compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26A, it is not necessary for the articles of the transferee company (or a draft of them) to be approved by ordinary resolution of the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed.
@ref s 912 The articles of the new transferee company, or a draft of them, must be approved by ordinary resolution of each of the transferor companies (src:12679-12680)
GIVEN `the scheme is a merger by formation of a new company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the compromise or arrangement is to be sanctioned under Part 26A and this is the company in respect of which it is proposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 282 the resolution approving the articles or a draft of them is an ordinary resolution of the transferor company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 912(1) the articles of the transferee company have been approved by ordinary resolution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the scheme is a merger by formation of a new company`) THEN `s 903(1) requirement does not apply` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a merger by formation of a new company"
        IF `the compromise or arrangement is to be sanctioned under Part 26A and this is the company in respect of which it is proposed` THEN `s 903(1) requirement does not apply` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not necessary for the articles of the transferee company (or a draft of them) to be approved by ordinary resolution of the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed"
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `s 282 the resolution approving the articles or a draft of them is an ordinary resolution of the transferor company`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 903(1) requirement complied with`
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` -- a bare "must" not done (fork F3)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 903(1) requirement not covered` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 282 is outside this range

§§ `Protection of holders of securities to which special rights attached (merger) (s 913)`

-- JURAL the holder of the securities: claim to rights of equivalent value in the transferee company | the scheme (and the transferee company): duty to provide them
-- src:12682 | (1) The scheme must provide that where any securities of a transferor company (other than shares) to which special rights are attached are held by a person otherwise than as a member or creditor of the company, that person is to receive rights in the transferee company of equivalent value.
-- src:12683 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if—
-- src:12684 | (a) the holder has agreed otherwise, or
-- src:12685 | (b) the holder is, or under the scheme is to be, entitled to have the securities purchased by the transferee company on terms that the court considers reasonable.
@ref s 913 The scheme must provide that holders of securities (other than shares) with special rights receive rights of equivalent value (src:12682-12685)
GIVEN `securities of a transferor company (other than shares) to which special rights are attached are held by a person otherwise than as a member or creditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder has agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder is, or under the scheme is to be, entitled to have the securities purchased by the transferee company on terms that the court considers reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme provides that the holder is to receive rights in the transferee company of equivalent value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 913(1) the scheme protects the holder of securities to which special rights are attached` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`securities of a transferor company (other than shares) to which special rights are attached are held by a person otherwise than as a member or creditor of the company`)
            THEN `s 903(1) requirement does not apply` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where any securities of a transferor company (other than shares) to which special rights are attached are held by a person otherwise than as a member or creditor"
        IF `the holder has agreed otherwise` OR `the holder is, or under the scheme is to be, entitled to have the securities purchased by the transferee company on terms that the court considers reasonable`
            THEN `s 903(1) requirement does not apply` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if— (a) the holder has agreed otherwise, or (b) the holder is, or under the scheme is to be, entitled to have the securities purchased"
        IF `the scheme provides that the holder is to receive rights in the transferee company of equivalent value`
            THEN `s 903(1) requirement complied with`
        OTHERWISE `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` -- a bare "must" not done (fork F3)

§§ `No allotment of shares to transferor company or its nominee (merger) (s 914)`

-- JURAL the members of the transferor companies: immunity from dilution by allotments to a company holding its own shares | the scheme: disability to provide for them
-- src:12687 | The scheme must not provide for any shares in the transferee company to be allotted to—
-- src:12688 | (a) a transferor company (or its nominee) in respect of shares in the transferor company held by the transferor company itself (or its nominee); or
-- src:12689 | (b) the transferee company (or its nominee) in respect of shares in a transferor company held by the transferee company (or its nominee).
@ref s 914 The scheme must not provide for shares in the transferee company to be allotted to a transferor company or its nominee, or to the transferee company or its nominee (src:12687-12689)
GIVEN `the scheme provides for shares in the transferee company to be allotted to a transferor company (or its nominee) in respect of shares in the transferor company held by the transferor company itself (or its nominee)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme provides for shares in the transferee company to be allotted to the transferee company (or its nominee) in respect of shares in a transferor company held by the transferee company (or its nominee)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 914 the scheme does not provide for the allotment of shares the section forbids` MEANS
    IF `the scheme provides for shares in the transferee company to be allotted to a transferor company (or its nominee) in respect of shares in the transferor company held by the transferor company itself (or its nominee)`
       OR `the scheme provides for shares in the transferee company to be allotted to the transferee company (or its nominee) in respect of shares in a transferor company held by the transferee company (or its nominee)`
    THEN `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The scheme must not provide for any shares in the transferee company to be allotted to"
    ELSE `s 903(1) requirement complied with`

