        IF `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 916(3A) subsection (3A) is satisfied`, `s 916(3B) subsection (3B) is satisfied`) EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer is not known and neither way is satisfied
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first condition is that either subsection (3A) or subsection (3B) is satisfied"

-- (4A): the members of the transferee company were able, during the period beginning one month before and ending on the date mentioned in (3A), to inspect the document at the registered office.
-- src:12725 | (4A) This subsection is satisfied for a document if the members of the transferee company were able during the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date mentioned in subsection (3A) to inspect that document at the registered office of that company.
@ref s 916(4A) The members of the transferee company were able to inspect the document at its registered office throughout the period (src:12725)
GIVEN `first day on which the members of the transferee company were able to inspect the document at its registered office` IS A DATE
      `last day on which the members of the transferee company were able to inspect the document at its registered office` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 916(4A) subsection (4A) is satisfied for the document` MEANS
    IF `s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day on which the members of the transferee company were able to inspect the document at its registered office` `last day on which the members of the transferee company were able to inspect the document at its registered office` `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection is satisfied for a document if the members of the transferee company were able during the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date mentioned in subsection (3A) to inspect that document at the registered office of that company"

-- src:12726 | (4B) This subsection is satisfied for a document if—
-- src:12727 | (a) the document is made available on a website which is maintained by or on behalf of the transferee company and identifies the company,
-- src:12728 | (b) access to the document on the website is not conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted, and
-- src:12729 | (c) the document remains available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date mentioned in subsection (3A).
@ref s 916(4B) The document was on the transferee company's website, free of fee and restriction, throughout the period (src:12726-12729)
GIVEN `the document is made available on a website which is maintained by or on behalf of the transferee company and identifies the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `access to the document on the website is conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `first day on which the document was continuously available on the website` IS A DATE
      `last day on which the document was continuously available on the website` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 916(4B) subsection (4B) is satisfied for the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is made available on a website which is maintained by or on behalf of the transferee company and identifies the company`
       AND (NOT (`access to the document on the website is conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted`))
       AND `s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day on which the document was continuously available on the website` `last day on which the document was continuously available on the website` `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection is satisfied for a document if— (a) the document is made available on a website which is maintained by or on behalf of the transferee company and identifies the company, (b) access to the document on the website is not conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted, and (c) the document remains available on the website throughout the period"

-- The documents are those listed in the applicable paragraphs of section 911(3)(a) to (f): one answer per document (the caller supplies the answer of (4A) or (4B) for each).
-- src:12724 | (4) The second condition is that subsection (4A) or (4B) is satisfied for each of the documents listed in the applicable paragraphs of section 911(3)(a) to (f) relating to the transferee company and the transferor company (or, if there is more than one transferor company, each of them).
