    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant securities”, in relation to a company, means shares or other securities carrying the right to vote at general meetings"

-- "it is not necessary for the scheme to be approved at a meeting ... if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with":
-- the court's satisfaction is a conditional input (fork F4); the four conditions are functions of the facts.
-- JURAL the members of the transferee company: immunity from being called to a meeting | the court: power to excuse the meeting on being satisfied
-- src:12717 | (2) It is not necessary for the scheme to be approved at a meeting of the members, or any class of members, of the transferee company if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with.
@ref s 916(2) It is not necessary for the scheme to be approved at a meeting of the members of the transferee company if the court is satisfied that the conditions have been complied with (src:12717)
GIVEN `s 916(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 916(3) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 916(4) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 916(4C) the third condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 916(5) the fourth condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 916(2) the meeting of members of the transferee company is not required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 916(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies in the case of a merger by absorption where"
        IF NOT (`the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) (LIST `s 916(3) the first condition is met`, `s 916(4) the second condition is met`, `s 916(4C) the third condition is met`, `s 916(5) the fourth condition is met`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the following conditions have been complied with" (a condition is not met)
        IF `s 916(1) this section applies` EQUALS NOTHING OR elem NOTHING (LIST `s 916(3) the first condition is met`, `s 916(4) the second condition is met`, `s 916(4C) the third condition is met`, `s 916(5) the fourth condition is met`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer is not known and none has failed
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

