§§ `Circumstances in which no meetings required (merger) (s 917)`


-- The first condition, first way (3A): the registrar published notice of receipt of the draft terms in respect of all the merging companies at least one month
-- before the date of the first meeting of members of the transferor company summoned to agree to the scheme.
-- src:12742 | (3A) This subsection is satisfied if publication of notice of receipt of the draft terms by the registrar took place in respect of all the merging companies at least one month before the date of the court's order.
@ref s 917(3A) Publication of notice of receipt of the draft terms took place at least one month before the first meeting of members of the transferor company (src:12742)
GIVEN `date the registrar published notice of receipt of the draft terms in respect of all the merging companies` IS A DATE
      `date of the court's order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 917(3A) subsection (3A) is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `s 906(3) the date one month before` `date of the court's order` AT LEAST `date the registrar published notice of receipt of the draft terms in respect of all the merging companies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection is satisfied if publication of notice of receipt of the draft terms by the registrar took place in respect of all the merging companies at least one month before the date of the first meeting"

-- src:12743 | (3B) This subsection is satisfied if—
-- src:12744 | (a) the conditions in section 906A(2) to (4) are met in respect of each of the merging companies,
-- src:12745 | (b) in each case, the registrar published the notice mentioned in subsection (4) of that section in the Gazette at least one month before the date of the court's order, and
-- src:12746 | (c) the draft terms remained available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, that date.
@ref s 917(3B) The first condition, second way: the website route (src:12743-12746)
GIVEN `s 906A(2) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 906A(3) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 906A(4) the third condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `date the registrar published the notice mentioned in section 906A(4) in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `date of the court's order` IS A DATE
      `first day on which the draft terms were continuously available on the website` IS A DATE
      `last day on which the draft terms were continuously available on the website` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 917(3B) subsection (3B) is satisfied` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) (LIST `s 906A(2) the first condition is met`, `s 906A(3) the second condition is met`, `s 906A(4) the third condition is met`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) the conditions in section 906A(2) to (4) are met in respect of all the merging companies" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
        IF `s 906(3) the date one month before` `date of the court's order` LESS THAN `date the registrar published the notice mentioned in section 906A(4) in the Gazette`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the registrar published the notice mentioned in subsection (4) of that section in the Gazette at least one month before the date of the first meeting"
        IF NOT (`s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day on which the draft terms were continuously available on the website` `last day on which the draft terms were continuously available on the website` `date of the court's order`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) the draft terms remained available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, that date"
        IF elem NOTHING (LIST `s 906A(2) the first condition is met`, `s 906A(3) the second condition is met`, `s 906A(4) the third condition is met`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known and none has failed
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

