-- JURAL the members of the transferee company: immunity from being called to a meeting | the court: power to excuse the meeting on being satisfied
-- src:12740 | (2) It is not necessary for the scheme to be approved at a meeting of the members, or any class of members, of any of the merging companies if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with.
@ref s 917(2) It is not necessary for the scheme to be approved at a meeting of the members of the transferee company if the court is satisfied that the conditions have been complied with (src:12740)
GIVEN `s 917(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 917(3) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 917(4) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 917(4C) the third condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 917(5) the fourth condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 917(2) the meeting of members of any of the merging companies is not required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 917(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies in the case of a merger by absorption where"
        IF NOT (`the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) (LIST `s 917(3) the first condition is met`, `s 917(4) the second condition is met`, `s 917(4C) the third condition is met`, `s 917(5) the fourth condition is met`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the following conditions have been complied with" (a condition is not met)
        IF `s 917(1) this section applies` EQUALS NOTHING OR elem NOTHING (LIST `s 917(3) the first condition is met`, `s 917(4) the second condition is met`, `s 917(4C) the third condition is met`, `s 917(5) the fourth condition is met`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer is not known and none has failed
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (1): a merger by absorption where ALL of the relevant securities of the transferor company (or of each of them) are held by or on behalf of the transferee company.
-- JURAL none (a rule fixing when the section applies)
-- src:12739 | (1) This section applies in the case of a merger by absorption where all of the relevant securities of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one transferor company, of each of them) are held by or on behalf of the transferee company.
@ref s 917(1) The section applies to a merger by absorption where all the relevant securities of the transferor company are held by the transferee company (src:12739)
GIVEN `the scheme is a merger by absorption` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all of the relevant securities of the transferor company (or of each of them) are held by or on behalf of the transferee company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 917(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the scheme is a merger by absorption` AND `all of the relevant securities of the transferor company (or of each of them) are held by or on behalf of the transferee company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies in the case of a merger by absorption where all of the relevant securities of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one transferor company, of each of them) are held by or on behalf of the transferee company"

§§ `Other circumstances in which meeting of members of transferor company not required (merger) (s 917A)`

-- JURAL the members of the transferor company: immunity from being called to a meeting | whoever proposes the scheme: no duty to put it to them
-- src:12763 | In the case of a compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26A, it is not necessary for the scheme to be approved by the members of the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed.
@ref s 917A In the case of a compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26A, it is not necessary for the scheme to be approved by the members of the company in respect of which it is proposed (src:12763)
GIVEN `the compromise or arrangement is to be sanctioned under Part 26A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 917A(1) the meeting of members of the transferor company is not required` MEANS
    IF `the compromise or arrangement is to be sanctioned under Part 26A` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26A, it is not necessary" (an unmet "in the case of": the 2026-11-05 "where" ruling)

§§ `Other circumstances in which meeting of members of transferee company not required (merger) (s 918)`

-- (instantiated from the twin block of Circumstances in which meeting of members of transferee company not required (merger) (s 916); see work/expand.py)
§§ `Other circumstances in which meeting of members of transferee company not required (merger) (s 918)`


-- The first condition, first way (3A): the registrar published notice of receipt of the draft terms in respect of the transferee company at least one month
-- before the date of the first meeting of members of the transferor company summoned to agree to the scheme.
-- src:12767 | (2A) This subsection is satisfied if publication of notice of receipt of the draft terms by the registrar took place in respect of the transferee company at least one month before the date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one transferor company, any of them) summoned for the purposes of agreeing to the scheme.
@ref s 918(2A) Publication of notice of receipt of the draft terms took place at least one month before the first meeting of members of the transferor company (src:12767)
GIVEN `date the registrar published notice of receipt of the draft terms in respect of the transferee company` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one, any of them) summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 918(2A) subsection (2A) is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `s 906(3) the date one month before` `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one, any of them) summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme` AT LEAST `date the registrar published notice of receipt of the draft terms in respect of the transferee company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection is satisfied if publication of notice of receipt of the draft terms by the registrar took place in respect of the transferee company at least one month before the date of the first meeting"

-- src:12768 | (2B) This subsection is satisfied if—
-- src:12769 | (a) the conditions in section 906A(2) to (4) are met in respect of the transferee company,
-- src:12770 | (b) the registrar published the notice mentioned in subsection (4) of that section in the Gazette at least one month before the date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one transferor company, any of them) summoned for the purposes of agreeing to the scheme, and
-- src:12771 | (c) the draft terms remained available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, that date.
@ref s 918(2B) The first condition, second way: the website route (src:12768-12771)
GIVEN `s 906A(2) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 906A(3) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 906A(4) the third condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `date the registrar published the notice mentioned in section 906A(4) in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one, any of them) summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme` IS A DATE
      `first day on which the draft terms were continuously available on the website` IS A DATE
      `last day on which the draft terms were continuously available on the website` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 918(2B) subsection (2B) is satisfied` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) (LIST `s 906A(2) the first condition is met`, `s 906A(3) the second condition is met`, `s 906A(4) the third condition is met`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) the conditions in section 906A(2) to (4) are met in respect of the transferee company" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
        IF `s 906(3) the date one month before` `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one, any of them) summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme` LESS THAN `date the registrar published the notice mentioned in section 906A(4) in the Gazette`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the registrar published the notice mentioned in subsection (3) of that section in the Gazette at least one month before the date of the first meeting"
        IF NOT (`s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day on which the draft terms were continuously available on the website` `last day on which the draft terms were continuously available on the website` `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one, any of them) summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) the draft terms remained available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, that date"
        IF elem NOTHING (LIST `s 906A(2) the first condition is met`, `s 906A(3) the second condition is met`, `s 906A(4) the third condition is met`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known and none has failed
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12766 | (2) The first condition is that either subsection (2A) or subsection (2B) is satisfied.
@ref s 918(2) The first condition: subsection (2A) or subsection (2B) is satisfied (src:12766)
GIVEN `s 918(2A) subsection (2A) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 918(2B) subsection (2B) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 918(2) the first condition is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 918(2A) subsection (2A) is satisfied`, `s 918(2B) subsection (2B) is satisfied`) EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 918(2A) subsection (2A) is satisfied`, `s 918(2B) subsection (2B) is satisfied`) EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer is not known and neither way is satisfied
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first condition is that either subsection (2A) or subsection (2B) is satisfied"

-- (4A): the members of the transferee company were able, during the period beginning one month before and ending on the date mentioned in (3A), to inspect the document at the registered office.
-- src:12773 | (3A) This subsection is satisfied for a document if the members of the transferee company were able during the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date of any such meeting as is mentioned in subsection (2A) to inspect that document at the registered office of that company.
@ref s 918(3A) The members of the transferee company were able to inspect the document at its registered office throughout the period (src:12773)
GIVEN `first day on which the members of the transferee company were able to inspect the document at its registered office` IS A DATE
      `last day on which the members of the transferee company were able to inspect the document at its registered office` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one, any of them) summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 918(3A) subsection (3A) is satisfied for the document` MEANS
    IF `s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day on which the members of the transferee company were able to inspect the document at its registered office` `last day on which the members of the transferee company were able to inspect the document at its registered office` `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one, any of them) summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection is satisfied for a document if the members of the transferee company were able during the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date mentioned in subsection (2A) to inspect that document at the registered office of that company"

-- src:12774 | (3B) This subsection is satisfied for a document if—
-- src:12775 | (a) the document is made available on a website which is maintained by or on behalf of the transferee company and identifies the company,
-- src:12776 | (b) access to the document on the website is not conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted, and
-- src:12777 | (c) the document remains available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date of any such meeting as is mentioned in subsection (2A).
@ref s 918(3B) The document was on the transferee company's website, free of fee and restriction, throughout the period (src:12774-12777)
GIVEN `the document is made available on a website which is maintained by or on behalf of the transferee company and identifies the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `access to the document on the website is conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `first day on which the document was continuously available on the website` IS A DATE
      `last day on which the document was continuously available on the website` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one, any of them) summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 918(3B) subsection (3B) is satisfied for the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is made available on a website which is maintained by or on behalf of the transferee company and identifies the company`
       AND (NOT (`access to the document on the website is conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted`))
       AND `s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day on which the document was continuously available on the website` `last day on which the document was continuously available on the website` `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one, any of them) summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection is satisfied for a document if— (a) the document is made available on a website which is maintained by or on behalf of the transferee company and identifies the company, (b) access to the document on the website is not conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted, and (c) the document remains available on the website throughout the period"

-- The documents are those listed in the applicable paragraphs of section 911(3)(a) to (f): one answer per document (the caller supplies the answer of (4A) or (4B) for each).
-- src:12772 | (3) The second condition is that subsection (3A) or (3B) is satisfied for each of the documents listed in the applicable paragraphs of section 911(3) relating to the transferee company and the transferor company (or, if there is more than one transferor company, each of them).
@ref s 918(3) The second condition: subsection (3A) or (4B) is satisfied for each of the documents listed in section 911(3)(a) to (f) (src:12772)
GIVEN `for each of the documents the answer of subsection (3A) or subsection (3B)` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 918(3) the second condition is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) `for each of the documents the answer of subsection (3A) or subsection (3B)`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second condition is that subsection (3A) or (4B) is satisfied for each of the documents listed in the applicable paragraphs of section 911(3)(a) to (f)"
        IF elem NOTHING `for each of the documents the answer of subsection (3A) or subsection (3B)`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a document's answer is not known and none has failed
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12778 | (3C) The third condition is that the members of the transferee company were able to obtain copies of the documents mentioned in subsection (3), or any part of those documents, on request and free of charge, throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date of any such meeting as is mentioned in subsection (2A).
@ref s 918(3C) The third condition: the members of the transferee company were able to obtain copies free of charge throughout the period (src:12778)
GIVEN `first day on which the members of the transferee company were able to obtain copies on request free of charge` IS A DATE
      `last day on which the members of the transferee company were able to obtain copies on request free of charge` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one, any of them) summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 918(3C) the third condition is met` MEANS
    IF `s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day on which the members of the transferee company were able to obtain copies on request free of charge` `last day on which the members of the transferee company were able to obtain copies on request free of charge` `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one, any of them) summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The third condition is that the members of the transferee company were able to obtain copies of the documents ... on request and free of charge, throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date mentioned in subsection (2A)"

-- src:12779 | (3D) For the purposes of subsection (3C)—
-- src:12780 | (a) section 911A(5) applies as it applies for the purposes of section 911(1)(b), and
-- src:12781 | (b) Part 4 of Schedule 5 (communications by means of a website) does not apply.
@ref s 918(3D) For the purposes of subsection (3C), section 911A(5) applies and Part 4 of Schedule 5 does not (src:12779-12781)
GIVEN `the purposes are those of subsection (3C)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 918(3D) section 911A(5) applies and Part 4 of Schedule 5 does not apply` MEANS
    IF `the purposes are those of subsection (3C)` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of subsection (3C)"

-- The fourth condition: members holding not less than 5% of the paid-up voting capital (excluding treasury shares) would have been able to require a meeting of each class, and none did.
-- src:12782 | (4) The fourth condition is that—
-- src:12783 | (a) one or more members of that company, who together held not less than 5% of the paid-up capital of the company which carried the right to vote at general meetings of the company (excluding any shares in the company held as treasury shares) would have been able, during that period, to require a meeting of each class of members to be called for the purpose of deciding whether or not to agree to the scheme, and
-- src:12784 | (b) no such requirement was made.
@ref s 918(4) The fourth condition: members holding 5% could have required a meeting of each class and no such requirement was made (src:12782-12784)
GIVEN `the percentage of the paid-up capital of the company which carried the right to vote at general meetings (excluding shares held as treasury shares) held together by the members who would have been able to require a meeting of each class to be called` IS A NUMBER
      `a requirement to call such a meeting was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 918(4) the fourth condition is met` MEANS
    IF `the percentage of the paid-up capital of the company which carried the right to vote at general meetings (excluding shares held as treasury shares) held together by the members who would have been able to require a meeting of each class to be called` AT LEAST 5
       AND NOT (`a requirement to call such a meeting was made`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The fourth condition is that— (a) one or more members of the transferee company, who together held not less than 5% of the paid-up capital ... would have been able, during that period, to require a meeting of each class of members to be called ..., and (b) no such requirement was made"


-- "it is not necessary for the scheme to be approved at a meeting ... if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with":
-- the court's satisfaction is a conditional input (fork F4); the four conditions are functions of the facts.
-- JURAL the members of the transferee company: immunity from being called to a meeting | the court: power to excuse the meeting on being satisfied
-- src:12765 | (1) In the case of any merger by absorption, it is not necessary for the scheme to be approved by the members of the transferee company if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with.
@ref s 918(1) It is not necessary for the scheme to be approved at a meeting of the members of the transferee company if the court is satisfied that the conditions have been complied with (src:12765)
GIVEN `s 918 the scheme is a merger by absorption` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 918(2) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 918(3) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 918(3C) the third condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 918(4) the fourth condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 918(1) the meeting of members of the transferee company is not required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 918 the scheme is a merger by absorption` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of any merger by absorption"
        IF NOT (`the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) (LIST `s 918(2) the first condition is met`, `s 918(3) the second condition is met`, `s 918(3C) the third condition is met`, `s 918(4) the fourth condition is met`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the following conditions have been complied with" (a condition is not met)
        IF `s 918 the scheme is a merger by absorption` EQUALS NOTHING OR elem NOTHING (LIST `s 918(2) the first condition is met`, `s 918(3) the second condition is met`, `s 918(3C) the third condition is met`, `s 918(4) the fourth condition is met`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer is not known and none has failed
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Agreement to dispense with reports etc (merger) (s 918A)`

-- JURAL the merging companies and their directors: immunity from the listed requirements | the members and holders of voting securities: power to dispense by agreement (all of them)
-- src:12786 | (1) If all members holding shares in, and all persons holding other securities of, the merging companies, being shares or securities that carry a right to vote in general meetings of the company in question, so agree, the following requirements do not apply.
@ref s 918A(1) If all members and holders of other voting securities of the merging companies so agree, the requirements do not apply (src:12786)
GIVEN `all members holding shares in, and all persons holding other securities of, the merging companies, being shares or securities that carry a right to vote in general meetings of the company in question, so agree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 918A(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement` MEANS
    IF `all members holding shares in, and all persons holding other securities of, the merging companies, being shares or securities that carry a right to vote in general meetings of the company in question, so agree`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If all members holding shares in, and all persons holding other securities of, the merging companies ... so agree, the following requirements do not apply" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))

DECLARE `s 918A(1A) requirement` IS ONE OF
    `s 918A(1A)(a)(i) the requirements of section 908 (directors' explanatory report)`
    `s 918A(1A)(a)(ii) the requirements of section 909 (expert's report)`
    `s 918A(1A)(a)(iii) the requirements of section 910 (supplementary accounting statement)`
    `s 918A(1A)(a)(iv) the requirements of section 911B (report on material changes of assets of merging company)`
    `s 918A(1A)(b) the requirements of section 911 (inspection of documents) so far as relating to any document required to be drawn up under sections 908, 909 or 910`
    `s 918A(1A) any other requirement`

-- src:12787 | (1A) The requirements that may be dispensed with under this section are—
-- src:12788 | (a) the requirements of—
-- src:12789 | (i) i)section 908 (directors' explanatory report),
-- src:12790 | (ii) section 909 (expert's report),
-- src:12791 | (iii) section 910 (supplementary accounting statement), and
-- src:12792 | (iv) section 911B (report on material changes of assets of merging company); and
-- src:12793 | (b) the requirements of section 911 (inspection of documents) so far as relating to any document required to be drawn up under sections 908, 909 or 910.
@ref s 918A(1A) The requirements that may be dispensed with (src:12787-12793)
GIVEN requirement IS A `s 918A(1A) requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 918A(1A) the requirement is one that may be dispensed with under section 918A` MEANS
    CONSIDER requirement
    WHEN `s 918A(1A) any other requirement` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The requirements that may be dispensed with under this section are" lists, and does not say "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 918A(3) Part under which the compromise or arrangement is to be sanctioned` IS ONE OF
    `s 918A(3)(a) Part 26`
    `s 918A(3)(b) Part 26A`

-- src:12798 | (3) In subsection (2) “the relevant application” means—
-- src:12799 | (a) in the case of a compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26, the application to the court under section 896;
-- src:12800 | (b) in the case of a compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26A, the application to the court under section 901C(1).
@ref s 918A(3) "the relevant application" (src:12798-12800)
GIVEN part IS A `s 918A(3) Part under which the compromise or arrangement is to be sanctioned`
      `date of the application to the court under section 896` IS A DATE
      `date of the application to the court under section 901C(1)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 918A(3) the date of the relevant application` MEANS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `s 918A(3)(a) Part 26` THEN `date of the application to the court under section 896`
    WHEN `s 918A(3)(b) Part 26A` THEN `date of the application to the court under section 901C(1)`

-- (2): the members and the holders of other securities, and whether shares or securities carry a right to vote, are determined as at the date of the relevant application.
-- src:12794 | (2) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:12795 | (a) the members, or holders of other securities, of a company, and
-- src:12796 | (b) whether shares or other securities carry a right to vote in general meetings of the company,
-- src:12797 | are determined as at the date of the relevant application.
@ref s 918A(2) The members, holders of other securities and voting rights are determined as at the date of the relevant application (src:12794-12797)
GIVEN `the date as at which the person's holding is stated` IS A DATE
      `the date of the relevant application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 918A(2) the holding counts for the purposes of section 918A` MEANS
    IF `the date as at which the person's holding is stated` EQUALS `the date of the relevant application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
